% AUTHOR: implementation-absys (an agent: Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5). One text for absys, absys-depth-first and absys-wake-back.
% PRECURSOR-SEEN: no. Not any E01-E09 program (see programs/absys/README.md, batch 1B, for what was read).
% NOTATION: 1969 (.ab1), the earliest notation with every construct used (systems/absys/README.md, Notation).
% IDIOM: a relation as name'=lambda x begin {A or B} end, primes for new names, lists [a;b] and [h&t], quoted constants 'a': Foster and Elcock 1969 (map and item, examples/map.ab1, examples/triples.ab1; tutorial ch. 8, ch. 10; docs/decisions.md rule 5);
% IDIOM: the head pattern of a case as an equation on the lambda's parameter: Elcock 1990 p. 8 (examples/append.abs).
% alist-right, P04 Vocabulary, in that order: case 1, alist(<>); case 2, alist(<A> ++ m) if alist(m), its head as an equation, then alist(m).
alist'=lambda p
    begin {p = [] or p = ['a'&m'] alist(m)} end
% P04f. Unknown s. One stage: alist(s), with alist-right. No constants.
% STAGE 1
alist(s)
